#!/bin/bash
# A PBS job (also a finished one): an overview, or the given attributes one per line in their order (an empty line when
# missing). Without an id, the job you are in (PBS_JOBID: a batch job, the shell of job-shell).
#
#   job-info                                         # the job you are in
#   job-info 1234567                                 # its state, node, resources, time and folders
#   job-info 1234567 job_state exec_host2 Output_Path   # `id` is the full job id; all attributes: qstat -xwf <id>

set -euo pipefail

if (( $# == 0 )) && [[ -z ${PBS_JOBID:-} ]]; then
    echo "usage: job-info [job-id [attribute...]] (without an id only in a job)" >&2
    exit 2
fi
id=${1:-$PBS_JOBID}
shift || true

# The attributes of the job, one per line. Plain `qstat -f` instead of `-F json`, whose escaping of the job's
# environment is not always valid JSON.
attributes() {
    qstat -x -w -f "$id" | python3 -c '
import sys

attrs, key = {}, None
for line in sys.stdin:
    line = line.rstrip("\n")
    if line.startswith("Job Id: "):
        attrs["id"] = line.removeprefix("Job Id: ")
    elif line.startswith("\t") and key:  # continuation of a long value
        attrs[key] += line.lstrip("\t")
    elif " = " in line:
        key, value = line.strip().split(" = ", 1)
        attrs[key] = value

for name in sys.argv[1:]:
    print(attrs.get(name, ""))
' "$@"
}

if (( $# > 0 )); then
    attributes "$@"
    exit
fi

# not $(…), it drops the empty lines of missing attributes; a failure of qstat (unknown job, its message goes to the
# terminal) leaves no id
mapfile -t f < <(attributes id Job_Name job_state exec_host2 Resource_List.select Resource_List.walltime \
    resources_used.walltime Variable_List comment)
if [[ -z ${f[0]} ]]; then
    exit 1
fi
var() {
    grep -o "$1=[^,]*" <<< "${f[7]}" | cut -d= -f2 || true
}
host=${f[3]%%[:+]*}
time="${f[6]:-0:00:00} of ${f[5]}"
if [[ ${f[2]} == R ]]; then
    IFS=: read -r wh wm ws <<< "${f[5]}"
    IFS=: read -r uh um us <<< "${f[6]:-0:0:0}"
    left=$(( (10#$wh - 10#$uh) * 3600 + (10#$wm - 10#$um) * 60 + 10#$ws - 10#$us ))
    time+=", ends $(date -d "+$left seconds" '+%Y-%m-%d %H:%M')"
fi
cat <<EOF
job ${f[0]%%.*}  ${f[1]}
  state      ${f[2]}${f[8]:+ (${f[8]})}
  node       ${host:--}
  resources  ${f[4]}
  time       $time
  scratch    $(var SCRATCHDIR)
  folder     $(var PBS_O_WORKDIR)
EOF
